 is held at its prior. Applying the fixed-point condition, if the other node stays at prior then my choice doesn't change its output, so defecting comes out ahead in both cases: 0 versus 2, and 4 versus 5. That leads me toward A\n\nThe edge question is the part to settle: the other copy's mechanism evaluates the agent's function on a different input, so it's a separate node and my choice doesn't feed into it. With that node held at prior, defecting is dominant, so the fixed point is submit-submit. This is a fictional game, so I'll just output the submit command.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working out the decision under the A-FDT reading, where each of the two copies has its own node tied to different observations. My copy's decision node is separate from the other copy's, which is held at its prior. Applying the fixed-point condition, if the other node stays at prior then my choice doesn't change its output, so defecting comes out ahead in both cases: 0 versus 2, and 4 versus 5. That leads me toward A\n\nThe edge question is the part to settle: the other copy's mechanism evaluates the agent's function on a different input, so it's a separate node and my choice doesn't feed into it. With that node held at prior, defecting is dominant, so the fixed point is submit-submit. This is a fictional game, so I'll just output the submit command.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10033,"completion_tokens":832,"total_tokens":10865,"cost":0.056772,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.056772,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.040132,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01664},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":324,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}